## Initial controller DTO finding

The current Core `api/controller.rs` exposes 41 distinct Rustdoc public names and RPC request coverage, but pinned Java 5.5.1 DTO behavior is incomplete: `BrokerReplicasInfo.addReplicaInfo` and three `ReplicasInfo.isExistIn*` methods have no Rust equivalents; Java `ReplicaIdentity.equals`/`hashCode` ignore `alive`; nullable map/list states and `BrokerMemberGroup.minimumBrokerId` null behavior need parity work. This session is addressing the observable DTO methods and preserving test evidence before changing the crosswalk.

## Controller DTO implementation and fixture

Implemented nullable map keys/values and list elements for the controller DTOs; `BrokerReplicasInfo::add_replica_info`; all three replica membership methods with Java `ArrayList.contains` equality, null failure, and short-circuit paths; `ReplicaIdentity::java_equals` and `java_hash_code` ignoring `alive`; Java `minimumBrokerId` null/error semantics; hash-code and `toString` mappings where the pinned Java classes override them; and `EpochEntry::from_entry` for the Java copy constructor. Removed structural equality traits from DTOs whose Java classes inherit identity equality.

Added `controllerDtoApi` and `controllerDtoOperations` to the pinned producer-core Java fixture. Regenerated `fixtures/producer/core.json`, SHA-256 `b45df3622bca04a1ea4ba93e5700abe235745908ea2342af4b6ad51ca75fdeb6`. Pinned source artifact SHA-256: `ac2d2ad39cbe35e2125ce8cfdd2dd1c20ff7007f9960c1c4b597e292123a6bf6`.

